sequenceDiagram
    title Diagram 2: Server startup, idle workers waiting, and wake-up
    actor C as Client
    participant M as Master thread
    participant B as Request buffer<br/>(bounded queue + mutex)

    activate M
    M->>M: parse -t threads -b buffers -s FIFO|SFF
    M->>+B: init(capacity = buffers), count = 0
    B-->>-M: ready
    create participant W1 as Worker 1
    M->>W1: pthread_create(worker_loop)
    create participant W2 as Worker 2
    M->>W2: pthread_create(worker_loop)
    Note over M,W2: ... one thread per -t, all created at start (fixed-size pool)

    W1->>B: lock(mutex)
    loop while count == 0
        W1->>B: wait(not_empty) - releases mutex and sleeps
    end
    W2->>B: lock(mutex)
    loop while count == 0
        W2->>B: wait(not_empty) - releases mutex and sleeps
    end
    Note over W1,W2: No busy-waiting: idle workers sleep on the condition variable

    M->>M: listen() and block in accept()
    C->>M: new connection
    M->>+B: lock, put(conn_fd), count = 1
    B--)W1: signal(not_empty) wakes exactly one worker
    M->>B: unlock(mutex)
    deactivate B
    deactivate M
    B-->>W1: wait() returns, mutex re-acquired, count = 1
    activate W1
    W1->>B: get() request, count = 0, unlock(mutex)
    W1->>W1: handle request (same as Diagram 1)
    W1->>C: response
    deactivate W1
    Note over W2: Worker 2 keeps sleeping because count is still 0
